==============================================================================
PART (c) -- THE CASSINI-vs-DEEP CONFLICT: does xi spoil the r^-2?
==============================================================================
  Deep regime (g_N << a0): the phantom is the exact r^-2 profile
  rho_ph(r) = sqrt(G M a0)/(4 pi G r^2)  (equipartition exactness).  The
  biharmonic adds the operator xi^2 Delta^2 to the static field equation.
  For the deep potential phi = A ln(r/r0), A = sqrt(G M a0):

      Delta phi = A/r^2,   Delta^2 phi = 2A/r^4

  so the phantom-density perturbation is EXACTLY

      delta rho/rho_ph = 2 (xi/r)^2   ->   0  as  r -> infinity.

  The lifted deep form keeps the r^-2 phantom up to O((xi/r)^2): the
  xi-scale is confined below ~pc and cannot corrupt the deep law.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
