      r =    0.10 kpc:  delta rho/rho_ph = 4.050e-07
      r =    1.00 kpc:  delta rho/rho_ph = 4.050e-09
      r =   10.00 kpc:  delta rho/rho_ph = 4.050e-11
      r =  100.00 kpc:  delta rho/rho_ph = 4.050e-13
  [PASS] C1 [DEEP FORM LIFTED] the biharmonic's correction to the r^-2 phantom
      is 2(xi/r)^2, decreasing in r and < 1e-3 everywhere above
      ~30 pc: the equipartition exactness survives
         measured: r=0.01 kpc: 4.1e-05; r=0.1 kpc: 4.0e-07; r=1 kpc: 4.1e-09; r=10 kpc: 4.1e-11; r=100 kpc: 4.0e-13
         threshold: delta rho/rho_ph -> 0 as r -> inf; <= 1e-3 above pc scales
         Numerically verified on the grid (radial laplacian/biharmonic of the
         deep logarithmic potential): Delta phi = A/r^2 and
         Delta^2 phi = 2A/r^4 to 1e-10.  At r = 1 kpc the phantom is
         spoiled at the 4e-9 level; at 10 kpc at 4e-11: unobservable.
